# Studio Marche — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. Never commit the real
# .env file — only this example should be in version control.
#
# This app uses Vite, which only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_
# to client-side code (see https://vite.dev/guide/env-and-mode). Since
# the Shopify Storefront API is designed to be called from the browser
# (its tokens are public/read-only by design), the variable names below
# use that prefix. If you later move Shopify fetching to a backend
# server instead, you can drop the VITE_ prefix there.
#
# ─── Shopify — one brand ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Minimal setup for a single connected brand. Uncomment and fill in to
# enable real data for that brand's storefront page.
#
# VITE_SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN=brand-name.myshopify.com
# VITE_SHOPIFY_STOREFRONT_ACCESS_TOKEN=shpat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ─── Shopify — multiple brands ─────────────────────────────────────────
# For each brand added to src/app/lib/shopify/sources.ts, add one token
# variable here matching the `accessTokenEnvVar` name you used there.
# Example, for a brand registered with accessTokenEnvVar
# "SHOPIFY_STUDIO_CLAY_ACCESS_TOKEN":
#
# VITE_SHOPIFY_STUDIO_CLAY_ACCESS_TOKEN=shpat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ─── Do not add ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never put a Shopify Admin API access token in a client-exposed (VITE_)
# variable. Admin tokens can read and write orders, customers, and
# payouts — they must only ever be used from a server you control.
# SHOPIFY_ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN is intentionally not used anywhere in this
# codebase for that reason.
